Depends: libc6 (>= LIBC_MIN), libgcc-s1, libstdc++6 (>= LIBSTDCXX_MIN), libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0, libjavascriptcoregtk-4.1-0, libsoup-3.0-0, libgtk-3-0t64 | libgtk-3-0, libgtk-layer-shell0, libayatana-appindicator3-1 | libappindicator3-1, libglib2.0-0t64 | libglib2.0-0, libcairo2, libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0 | libgdk-pixbuf2.0-0, libdbus-1-3, libssl3t64 | libssl3, libasound2t64 | libasound2, libopenblas0, libvulkan1, xdotool, wtype, wl-clipboard
Recommends: ydotool
Description: offline speech-to-text desktop application
 Handy is a free, open source and extensible speech-to-text application that
 works completely offline. Press a global shortcut, speak, and the
 transcription is pasted into whichever application has focus. Speech is
 recognised locally with Whisper, Parakeet and other models, so no audio ever
 leaves the machine.
 .
 The command is handy. It runs on X11 and Wayland; xdotool, wtype and
 wl-clipboard are pulled in so text can be typed and pasted in either session,
 plus ydotool where the suite has it (needed on GNOME Wayland).
 Models are downloaded from inside the app on first use.
